Add-on: --spec-draft-head-subset N. The MTP draft steps read the output head once per drafted token; when the head is in host memory that is
the biggest cost of a draft step. This keeps the first N rows (the most frequent tokens of a BPE vocabulary) and the last 1024 rows (special tokens)
of the head in device memory and lets the draft choose among them. The target model still verifies every token with the full head, so the output
is exact. Only the draft context uses it; off by default.
Requires: 0003-moe-cache-cpu-miss-prewarm-and-adaptive-draft.patch

